<div id="outline-container-orga358455" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orga358455"><a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/feed/index.xml#orga358455">Going forward</a></h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-orga358455">
<p>
I finished my consulting contract lately, so it'll be interesting to see how to manage my finances when I'm living completely off savings and investments. There's a bit more paperwork because I have to go figure out adjusted cost bases, but I think I'll be able to get the hang of it. I don't think it's going to change my time allocation very much, because my consulting was down to about two hours or so a week. But now I don't have to worry about accidentally missing a message or making sure that I can figure out my old code enough to implement a request. It was nice to get to a good solid end. The client was very happy with my work, and I was very happy with how that whole thing turned out.
</p>

<p>
With my interest in practicing French and getting the hang of talking out loud,
I've been playing around with speech recognition a lot more. I'm happy to find that the local speech recognition models have actually gotten pretty good. I've been experimenting a lot with speech recognition and voice commands in Emacs. I'm looking forward to exploring that this year.
</p>

<p>
I've been sharing more of those experiments through live streams. It's one of those things that it's hard to get a sense of when you're just reading it off a blog post or code. That's been going well too, because I like the kinds of conversations I have and the ideas that people share.
</p>

<p>
I also like how we've been getting more involved with safe streets advocacy in Toronto.
I'd like to see what we can do to help.
Even as it feels like the outside world is getting crazier and crazier,
I've been lucky enough to meet a lot of people who have their head on straight
and who are trying to make things better. I want to help.
</p>

<p>
We'll see how it goes.
We'll see how we grow.
</p>
